        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(safeguard): resolve compaction provider/model before registering runtime",
        "body": "Fixes #57901.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nSafeguard auto-compaction registered and preferred the active session model even when `agents.defaults.compaction.model` selected a different summarization model. That made the documented override ineffective in normal embedded runs. A cross-provider override could also resolve its model descriptor without binding profile-only credentials into the provider-keyed runtime auth storage, causing the safeguard to cancel when it later requested auth.\n\n## Summary\n\nSafeguard auto-compaction now resolves and prepares the configured compaction target before synchronous extension registration.\n\n- Reuse `resolveEmbeddedCompactionTarget` before safeguard registration.\n- Resolve the selected provider/model through the active `ModelRegistry`, including alias/configured-model support.\n- Resolve target-provider auth from the active `AuthProfileStore`, apply provider runtime auth/base-URL/request overrides, and bind the resulting credential into `AuthStorage` before registering the safeguard.\n- Share that auth preparation contract with explicit `/compact` instead of maintaining a second inline implementation.\n- Keep `buildEmbeddedExtensionFactories` synchronous by passing it a precomputed safeguard target.\n- Prefer the registered compaction model over `ctx.model` inside the safeguard hook.\n- Preserve locked native-harness sessions on their pinned model.\n- When a configured override cannot be resolved or authenticated, emit a precise warning and retain the active session model instead of registering an unusable target.\n- Use the resolved compaction model's context window.\n- Remove the PR-only proof script and unrelated collateral churn.\n\n## Behavior\n\nFor a normal embedded run, the configured compaction target is resolved through the same shared resolver used by explicit compaction. A provider switch intentionally drops the session provider's profile ID, then selects the target provider's configured profile order/store. The resolved model, selected profile, provider runtime request overrides, and bound runtime credential travel together into safeguard registration.\n\nFor explicit `/compact`, the shared auth helper prepares the target model and credential once. Registration receives the effective prepared model. If selection is locked to a native harness, the configured override remains intentionally ignored.\n\nThe safeguard hook uses:\n\n```ts\nconst model = runtime?.model ?? ctx.model;\n```\n\nThat lets a configured compaction model win while preserving the active model as the no-override, unresolved-target, or missing-target-auth fallback.\n\n## Evidence\n\nValidated on the synchronized merge tree:\n\n- PR head: `ecfc4491ece04b29ccb48c42ecb6a40d6e0d8a37`\n- Main cutoff / merge ancestry: `262baedcf7fa3d66dc35cce7d0253e0a31f0cc0e`\n- Final diff: 9 files, +623/-75\n\nChecks:\n\n- Core TypeScript project — passed\n- Core test TypeScript project — passed\n- Compaction-focused Vitest batch — 8 files, 464 tests passed\n- Run-attempt support consumers — 12 files, 190 tests passed\n- Profile-only cross-provider regression uses real in-memory stores: Anthropic is active in `AuthStorage`; the OpenAI compaction key exists only in `AuthProfileStore`; preparation binds it so `ModelRegistry.getApiKeyAndHeaders` succeeds\n- Missing-target-auth regression verifies warning, active-model fallback, and no target runtime credential\n- `oxfmt --check` and targeted `oxlint` on the seven newly touched files — passed\n- `git diff --check` — passed\n\nThe previous exact head also passed the full GitHub CI matrix after its same-tree retrigger. This head requires a fresh exact-head CI and ClawSweeper review.\n\n## Testing scope\n\nNo live provider API call was made. Regression coverage exercises target resolution, provider-switch auth selection/binding, prepared runtime model registration, native-harness model locking, unresolved/missing-auth fallback, and the safeguard summarizer receiving the runtime-selected model. Real provider-backed automatic-compaction proof remains an external maintainer/environment gate.",
